      "text": "IN PHOTOS: Workers carry out repainting and renovation works at the historic Manila Central Post Office on Thursday, May 28, 2026, as rehabilitation efforts continue following the massive fire that damaged the landmark building in 2023. The then 97-year-old Manila Central Post Office building was razed by fire on this day in 2023. The building was declared Important Cultural Property in 2018. It is now undergoing restoration efforts and is poised to be a tourist destination once finished, according to PHLpost. \n\n📸: Norman Cruz",
